## Why This Is Asked
Tests automated incident response playbooks for cross-region database replication failures and data integrity under pressure. Emphasizes signal quality, containment, sequencing, rollback, and validation.

## Key Concepts
- Incident response runbooks across AWS accounts and regions
- DynamoDB Global Tables consistency, point-in-time recovery, and backups
- Event-driven automation with EventBridge and Step Functions
- Safe containment with SSM Automation and IAM boundaries
- Testing via controlled chaos experiments and audit trails

## Code Example
```json
{
  "Comment": "DR workflow for DynamoDB Global Tables replication failure",
  "StartAt": "DetectReplicationLag",
  "States": {
    "DetectReplicationLag": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::lambda:invoke",
      "Parameters": {
        "FunctionName": "check-dynamodb-replication"
      },
      "Next": "ContainIncident"
    },
    "ContainIncident": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::aws-sdk:ssm:startAutomationExecution",
      "Parameters": {
        "DocumentName": "isolate-dynamodb-region"
      },
      "Next": "ValidateDataIntegrity"
    },
    "ValidateDataIntegrity": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "Variable": "$.validationResult",
          "StringEquals": "PASS",
          "Next": "FailoverToHealthyRegion"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "RollbackAndAlert"
    }
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
This tests practical crisis remediation for CRR failures, IAM drift, and automated recovery in a multi-account data lake.

## Key Concepts
- S3 Cross-Region Replication and troubleshooting
- IAM role trust policies and least privilege
- CloudWatch metrics/logs and alarms
- Safe rollback and data-consistency validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Node.js: fetch and inspect CRR configuration for a bucket
const { S3Client, GetBucketReplicationConfigurationCommand } = require('@aws-sdk/client-s3');
const c = new S3Client({region:'us-east-1'});
async function inspectCRR(bucketName) {
  const cmd = new GetBucketReplicationConfigurationCommand({Bucket: bucketName});
  const config = await c.send(cmd);
  console.log('CRR Role:', config.ReplicationConfiguration.Role);
  console.log('Rules:', config.ReplicationConfiguration.Rules);
  return config;
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses advanced DR design across multiple AWS services, cross-account governance, data consistency, testing rigor, and rollback plans under real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts

- Route 53 failover routing and health checks
- AWS Global Accelerator for fast global routing
- DynamoDB global tables for cross-region writes
- S3 cross-region replication for assets
- IAM boundary policies and per-region KMS keys
- Step Functions / Lambda for orchestration and playbooks
- DR testing, rollback, and cost controls

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal Step Functions skeleton for DR orchestration (pseudo-structure)
{
  "Comment": "DR failover workflow",
  "StartAt": "HealthCheck",
  "States": {
    "HealthCheck": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:REGION:ACCOUNT:function:HealthCheck",
      "Next": "Evaluate"
    },
    "Evaluate": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        { "Variable": "$.outage", "BooleanEquals": true, "Next": "InitiateFailover" }
      ],
      "Default": "Done"
    },
    "InitiateFailover": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:states:::aws-sdk:route53:changeResourceRecordSets",
      "End": true
    },
    "Done": { "Type": "Succeed" }
  }
}
```

